#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2fda9c8-7ae1-583d-b5b0-3f8105d5c35a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310916} {:answer/id #uuid "bc48d304-5608-59c0-bf0f-212e59aadf15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310917} {:answer/id #uuid "c83e22f8-b3de-5a66-95b9-bd18ffb596c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310918} {:answer/id #uuid "56453ca0-b56d-5a07-8753-b14af48c034c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310919} {:answer/id #uuid "2e646f1d-ceb6-5b3c-b5f0-781f2f09a1e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c83e22f8-b3de-5a66-95b9-bd18ffb596c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310918} :answer-field/id #uuid "55b49f2f-315e-50d2-ab17-0103385b9d24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5573f21-e824-5c9e-8e76-3403856afb46" :question/math-academy-id "q-130684" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $D=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}].$  Find $f(D)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-4 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-4I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(D)={D}^{2}-4I.$ \n\nLet's calculate ${D}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(D):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(D) & ={D}^{2}-4I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4-4 & 0+0 \\\\ 0+0 & 4-4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
